{"obsah":"<p>Today we broke our record for the number of riders deployed (not counting side programmes at trade fairs). Vlasta, Martin Šimůnek, kids from the club and Tobík Dolák went on bikes to the Festival of Records in Pelhřimov, which was celebrating its founding anniversary. On a motorbike there was Dalibor Šulc, plus parkour athletes Ondra and Honza from Flow Vision. Lukáš Valný and Michal Budský were busy at a corporate event in Žatec.</p>\n\n<p>The festival itself nailed the weather, and in almost 28 degrees records were broken all day, concerts took place and you could try out lots of attractions. Our team was placed right next to the main stage, and our task in 3 main 40-minute&nbsp; shows was both to perform and to set new Czech records. We left the first show without records but made it longer. In the second show Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček and Honza Daleký set a record in the standing long jump – Honza with feet together and Vlasta from back wheel to back wheel between two obstacles. Together that gave the guys 5.6 metres in the final attempts. Honza also set a standing jump record for parkour. Vlasta didn't beat his existing Czech record.<br>The last, shortest show at the end of the event was dedicated to Dalibor Šulc's record attempt: he set a Czech record for spins on the back wheel – 6 spins on the spot on the back wheel in 36 seconds.<br>We gave the shows our all and unfortunately not without injuries. First, parkour athlete Ondra broke a metatarsal bone in his foot, but neither the spectators nor the rest of us noticed anything until he started complaining about pain in his foot. Our youngest rider, Márty Kabeláč, fooled around on the back wheel for so long that he hit his nose and left an indelible pool of blood on Pelhřimov square. But by the last show he was back on the bike. Among other things, there was also a workshop for visitors.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4271.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4271.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250829\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4277.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4277.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250830\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4496.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4496.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250832\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4500.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4500.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250833\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4304.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F06%2FIMG_4304.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-250834\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"